id: power-regulation
name: Power Regulation
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Concealment
requiresSkill: concealment
requiresRanks: 2
# "Session Limit: Unlimited."
sessionLimit: unlimited
timeCost: N/A
# "You may freely gain or lose stacks of Holding Back." The Holding Back Maneuver's own question: a new
# total, from nothing to the base Tier of Power.
regulates: holding-back
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Gain or lose stacks of Holding Back at will, outside a Combat Encounter - and choose, entering one,
  whether they stay.
text: >
  Power Regulation: You adjust your detectable strength, concealing or revealing it at-will.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Concealment
  –Session Limit: Unlimited
  –Time Cost: N/A
  –Effect: You may freely gain or lose stacks of Holding Back. When entering a Combat Encounter, you
  choose if you maintain or lose these stacks of Holding Back.

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Concealment, with no Session Limit. Used: the
# Holding Back Maneuver's window, and the stacks set - nothing said in chat, since hiding one's strength
# is the point. Entering a Combat Encounter clears every Resource; one who held Holding Back stacks
# gets a card - Keep them, or Lose them - and keeping puts them back (combat.mjs startEncounter).
